Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:33:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/76] V.3 fault hook round 2 (Astra fault-hook R1 findings
 1-6): stdlib singleton vllm_ple_test_fault with dedicated O_NONBLOCK marker
 log (failed write suppresses the fault), explicit per-site eligibility and
 counting units, impossible selectors rejected, dropped D2H events retained,
 exc_async_output hooked on the PP0 relay path with sample_tokens under the
 PLE fatal boundary, acknowledged gates (publish-ack park, GIL-releasing FIFO
 for reconstruction/import, send-entry log), partial READY header cut (Sol
 draft, Fable applied/tested)

Fable fixups: disarmed async-output site checks _FAULT before reading progress state; stale round-1 test fixtures updated to the round-2 contract; site-count test now checks every fires() call is behind the None check; launch-deadline test reads only its own result line (send-entry log shares stdout).

Tests: tests/v1/ple_offload green (see log). Harness faultcut.sh/faultcut_eval.py kept outside the repo.
